fix(#38): make the component showcase page an accurate, exercised inventory

Per issue #38, epic #28's integration checkpoint covering #33-#37:

Radix UI retirement confirmed by search (not assumption): no file under
src/ imports any @radix-ui/* package directly. @radix-ui/react-accordion
and @radix-ui/react-collapsible remain in package.json as transitive needs
of @fumadocs/base-ui's own native Accordion/Collapsible (confirmed via its
own package.json), not local usage -- left untouched, since removing them
is a dependency-tree decision outside this ticket's scope and they aren't
imported by anything under src/.

GitHub Actions "Deploy Website" workflow: confirmed unmodified against the
fixed point (only pnpm install / pnpm build / aws s3 sync, unchanged).

pnpm exec tsc --noEmit and pnpm exec eslint . both clean (0 errors, one
pre-existing unrelated warning in postcss.config.mjs).

pnpm dev smoke check (via direct HTTP requests -- no browser available in
this sandbox) exercised home, /docs, /docs/components, /docs/atelier(+
teil-1), /docs/xeniapolis(+fuehrung): all 200, no server errors. Confirmed
data-section="xeniapolis" wraps DocsLayout+Footer (chrome included) only
on xeniapolis pages, and is absent on atelier/home pages -- section-scoped
theming doesn't leak. Confirmed the sidebar tab-switcher's two icons
resolve --atelier-color/--xeniapolis-color independently, per
src/app/docs/[[...slug]]/layout.tsx, and neither is redefined inside the
xeniapolis scope, so both stay visually distinct always (globals.css's own
documented intent). Dark-mode CSS (.dark and .dark [data-section=
'xeniapolis']) read correctly; toggling it live wasn't verifiable without
a browser.

While smoke-checking, found the component showcase page
(src/content/docs/components.mdx) did not actually exercise several
behaviors this ticket's own acceptance criteria call for, confirmed by
reading the installed @fumadocs/base-ui source under node_modules rather
than assuming from its .d.ts alone:

- Accordion had no `id`, so its copy-link button never rendered (only
  expand/collapse was exercisable) -- accordion.js only renders the
  CopyButton `if (id)`.
- Banner used `type="note"`, which isn't a real prop (Banner only accepts
  `variant`, `'normal' | 'rainbow'`), and had no `id`, so its dismiss
  button never rendered -- banner.js only renders it and persists to
  localStorage `if (id)`.
- Card had no `href`, so no link/navigation was exercisable at all.
- Tabs had none of `groupId`/`persist`/`updateAnchor` set -- the exact
  props #36 added -- and nothing anywhere else in the repo exercises them
  either, so cross-block sync, reload persistence, and URL-hash anchoring
  were entirely unexercised.
- `Slides` was imported but never rendered (a stale import); `Illu`, the
  illustration-gallery counterpart to `Slide`, wasn't imported at all
  despite being a real, actively-used component (besuch-in-der-
  wissensstadt.mdx, kurzuebersicht.mdx).

Fixed by adding the `id`s Accordion/Banner need, fixing Banner's prop,
replacing the non-linking Card with a `<Cards>` grid holding one internal
link (/docs/atelier) and one external link (this repo's own GitHub
remote, verified via `git remote -v`, not fabricated), adding a second
Tabs block sharing the first's groupId to demonstrate the sync, and adding
two Slide and two Illu instances (a single instance of either doesn't
read as a "gallery", which is what this ticket's smoke-check line asks
for). The illustration slug initially picked
(illustration-aufbruch-zum-kontinent-der-loesungen) turned out to
reference a pre-existing missing image file in public/illus/ -- the only
such gap across illus.json -- caught by checking the file exists on disk
before use, swapped for a working slug instead of fixing that unrelated
data bug.

Not fixed (noted, not touched -- outside this ticket's showcase-page
scope): `OverviewCards` (@/components/overview-cards) is imported in
src/content/docs/index.mdx and xeniapolis/index.mdx but rendered in
neither -- a genuinely stale import, confirmed by a repo-wide grep with
zero render sites -- but deciding whether to wire it up or delete the
component is a design call for a dedicated ticket, not this one.

Not verified: `pnpm build` could not be run to completion in this sandbox.
It's OOM-killed (SIGKILL, no heap-error trace) at "Creating an optimized
production build" regardless of Turbopack vs webpack, a reduced
--max-old-space-size, or --experimental-build-mode=compile.
--debug-build-paths scoped to just the home route builds cleanly with
memory to spare; --experimental-debug-memory-usage shows the crash
happens before the first JS-heap report, i.e. in the bundler's native
compilation of the ~53-page MDX content set, not the JS heap. This
sandbox has 1.9GB RAM, no swap, and no root to add any (swapon: Operation
not permitted) -- judged to be this container's resource ceiling, not a
defect from #33-#37, since the same build step is what "Deploy Website"
runs on a GitHub Actions runner with far more memory. Separately, an
OOM-killed build or dev run leaves a corrupted persistent Turbopack cache
under .next/ that produces a misleading stale-import error
(fumadocs-ui/css/neutral.css, a pre-#33 import) on the next run; clearing
.next/dev and .next/cache before restarting resolved it every time it
came up during this session's testing.

Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
EOF
)")
