Working tree is clean of build artifacts, and the change is committed at `5d23f7f`.

## Summary

For issue #38 (integrate-and-verify ticket for epic #28's component/theming refactor):

- **Radix retirement**: confirmed by grep — no file under `src/` imports `@radix-ui/*` directly.
- **GitHub Actions workflow**: confirmed unmodified against the fixed point.
- **tsc + eslint**: both clean.
- **Manual smoke check**: done via direct HTTP requests (no browser available in this sandbox) plus reading the installed `@fumadocs/base-ui` source to verify each component's actual prop-driven behavior. Confirmed Xeniapolis section-scoping (`data-section="xeniapolis"` wraps chrome, doesn't leak to Atelier/home pages) and the tab-switcher's two independently-resolved icon colors.
- **Component showcase page fix** (the actual code change, `src/content/docs/components.mdx`): found via smoke-testing that it didn't exercise several of this ticket's own required behaviors — Accordion's copy-link and Banner's dismiss button never rendered (missing `id`; Banner also used a nonexistent `type` prop), Card had no link, and Tabs never exercised `groupId`/`persist`/`updateAnchor` (added by #36 but unused anywhere in the repo). Fixed all of these, added a real internal+external Card grid (external link is this repo's own GitHub remote, not fabricated), and added genuine two-item Slide/Illu galleries — catching and swapping out one illustration slug that referenced a pre-existing missing image asset. Ran this through the code-review skill (Standards + Spec sub-agents in parallel) and fixed the two real findings it surfaced (a fabricated "gallery" that wasn't one, and a dead-weight unused-import render).
- **Not fixed, documented only**: `OverviewCards` is imported-but-unrendered in two unrelated content pages — a real stale import, but outside this ticket's showcase-page scope, left for a dedicated ticket.
- **Not verified**: `pnpm build` could not complete in this sandbox — OOM-killed at the bundler's native-compilation stage regardless of Turbopack/webpack/heap-size settings, on a 1.9GB-RAM, no-swap, no-root container. Isolated single-route builds succeed cleanly, and memory profiling shows the crash predates any JS-heap threshold, pointing at a sandbox resource ceiling rather than a defect — but this is the one acceptance-criteria box I couldn't literally check off myself.

